1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:06,640
The main idea of the project was to explore how, through the pretext of renovating built heritage,

2
00:00:08,039 --> 00:00:09,740
we could also contribute to urban improvement.

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,240
This here is the old rampart walkway.

4
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,040
It is essentially a kind of belvedere.

5
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:16,100
You have a view over the Aveyron river below,

6
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:18,020
you can see the valley,

7
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:22,260
and it gives you a broader understanding of the village as a whole,

8
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:25,300
because the village itself is medieval in structure.

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:28,720
In fact, there are not many places within the village center

10
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,200
where you can enjoy an open view.

11
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:32,740
There was no direct access to the garden.

12
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:36,700
The garden was connected only to the presbytery building.

13
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,500
So the idea was to create a new access point.

14
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:41,240
These stairs did not exist before.

15
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:43,600
And also to improve circulation.

16
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:46,640
In other words, to create a new pathway through the village.

17
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:50,040
So from the main street,

18
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:52,280
which is the village’s main axis,

19
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,400
you can now reach this garden through the narrow lane.

20
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:57,180
This garden acts almost like a hinge

21
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:00,420
allowing access to the street below as well,

22
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:04,140
in a very natural and intuitive way for people to use.

23
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:07,580
The idea was for it to become a new public space within the village center.

24
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:09,000
And above all, a garden.

25
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:13,240
It is quite a unique garden because it lies within the village walls,

26
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:15,160
yet remains open toward the landscape beyond.

27
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:19,320
The mill is also something quite important in the village.

28
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:22,520
It is a very beautiful building with strong heritage value,

29
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:25,280
which was restored by another architect

30
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:28,840
who carried out a remarkable intervention on the old tower, which had twisted

31
00:01:29,030 --> 00:01:31,160
during a storm and was therefore rebuilt in timber.

32
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:34,480
All of this contributes to creating a very interesting urban setting.

33
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:36,840
You can also see the bell tower behind the presbytery building.

34
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:40,920
Attached to it is a much older 15th-century building

35
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:43,540
which over time had been converted into a garage.

36
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:48,340
The project here was to restore it as a living space once again.

37
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,080
Today, all the apartments are occupied and rented out.

38
00:01:52,540 --> 00:02:02,120
There are three apartments in the presbytery building, one on each floor, and a duplex in the former chapel-garage, which once served a dual function.

39
00:02:04,659 --> 00:02:11,260
The purpose of the project was to highlight and enhance what already existed, to work with what was already there.

40
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:23,200
It is rewarding work because with relatively small interventions, it becomes possible to improve the living environment of the residents.